@meta{crate: motem, dependencies: list(motem-syntax, serde_motem), dependents: list(tomet-cli)}

=[motem]

==[motem]

The data language dual to tomet (`tmt` / `mtm`): a lightweight, expressive
syntax for values, maps and sequences. This is the crate to depend on when
using motem from Rust. It holds no logic of its own.

==[Overview]

- `syntax` is the language: parser, printer and the spelling helpers

(`motem-syntax`). Read its crate doc for what motem accepts.

- The top level is the serde side (`serde_motem`): [`from_str`] and

[`to_string`] read and write Rust types as motem.

A crate that sits below this one in the workspace layering (the tomet
parser, the printers) depends on `motem-syntax` directly.
